      "seed": 1037756158,
      "version": 2288,
      "versionNonce": 1360416738,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791801227904,
      "created": 1791793668593,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep dive\n\n1. How to ensure low latency for searching?\n- ES + CDC\n\n2. How to keep consistency of booking tickets? \n- update ... where ... (CAS)\n\n3. How to update ticket status?\n- ticket status (available | reserved | booked) + Cron -> stale (cron's period)\n- ticket status (available | reserved | booked) + reservedTimestamp -> good\n- ticket status (available | booked) + Redis lock -> lost reserved when redis down\n\n4. How to deal with surge traffic? (APIGateway - Nignx horizontal scale)\n- database CAS: 0 ~ 10k\n- redis lock + database CAS: 10k ~ 100k (single redis instance); > 100k (redis cluster) -> lost reserved when redis down\n- redis sorted set (ranking) + database CAS: > 100k (ZADD, ZRANK, SSE, queue + admited)\n\n5. How to support booking multiple tickets?\n\n- book ticket\nPOST /tickets/reserve/ -> 200 OK\nHeader: JWT token | session (userId)\nBody: {\n    ticketIds[]\n}\n\nPOST /tickets/confirm -> 200 OK\nHeader: JWT token | session (userId)\nBody: {\n    ticketIds[],\n    paymentIntent,\n}\n\nBooking \n- id\n- ticketIds[]\n- status: pending | confirmed\n- ...\n\nTicket\n- ...\n- bookingId\n- ...\n\n- reserve\nBEGIN;\nINSERT booking ...\nUPDATE ticket ... WHERE ... (ORDER BY ticketId to avoid dead locking)\nCOMMIT;\n\n- book\n...",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep dive\n\n1. How to ensure low latency for searching?\n- ES + CDC\n\n2. How to keep consistency of booking tickets? \n- update ... where ... (CAS)\n\n3. How to update ticket status?\n- ticket status (available | reserved | booked) + Cron -> stale (cron's period)\n- ticket status (available | reserved | booked) + reservedTimestamp -> good\n- ticket status (available | booked) + Redis lock -> lost reserved when redis down\n\n4. How to deal with surge traffic? (APIGateway - Nignx horizontal scale)\n- database CAS: 0 ~ 10k\n- redis lock + database CAS: 10k ~ 100k (single redis instance); > 100k (redis cluster) -> lost reserved when redis down\n- redis sorted set (ranking) + database CAS: > 100k (ZADD, ZRANK, SSE, queue + admited)\n\n5. How to support booking multiple tickets?\n\n- book ticket\nPOST /tickets/reserve/ -> 200 OK\nHeader: JWT token | session (userId)\nBody: {\n    ticketIds[]\n}\n\nPOST /tickets/confirm -> 200 OK\nHeader: JWT token | session (userId)\nBody: {\n    ticketIds[],\n    paymentIntent,\n}\n\nBooking \n- id\n- ticketIds[]\n- status: pending | confirmed\n- ...\n\nTicket\n- ...\n- bookingId\n- ...\n\n- reserve\nBEGIN;\nINSERT booking ...\nUPDATE ticket ... WHERE ... (ORDER BY ticketId to avoid dead locking)\nCOMMIT;\n\n- book\n...",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "biGtQ6TB2u9Ohw5ozZeDs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1975.606950380648,
      "y": 76.21441633018713,
